{"explanation":"Update MasterKey to create newly generated records with the persistent AndroidKeyStore-backed current wrapping key while retaining PBKDF2-derived keys exclusively for legacy-record reads. The existing public generate and decrypt entry points and their checked-exception contracts remain unchanged.","review_assumptions":["The coordinated Encryptor change uses the same AndroidKeyStore alias, "currentMasterKey", and compatible AES/GCM KeyGenParameterSpec settings, allowing current records created by either lifecycle to resolve the same persistent key.","android.security.keystore APIs are available to this Android production source at the module-supported API level.","A missing current wrapping-key alias while reading a current record is an unrecoverable key-resolution error and must not silently generate a replacement key."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","original_code":"import java.io.IOException;
